<code>assert !c.isEmpty() => \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < this.size(); this.get(i).equals(c.toArray()[i]);</code>

This assert statement checks that for every valid index `i` in the newly constructed `LinkedList`, the element at that index in the list is equal to the element at the same index in the input collection `c`. The condition `!c.isEmpty()` ensures that the collection is not empty, as the `toArray()` method would return an empty array otherwise, leading to potential `ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException`. However, since the comment specifies "for every valid index 'i' in this list," we assume that the list is non-empty when the collection is non-empty.
--------------------
<code>assert \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < this.size(); this.get(i).equals(c.toArray()[i]);</code>

This assert statement ensures that for every valid index `i` in the newly constructed `LinkedList`, the element at index `i` in the list is equal to the element at index `i` in the collection `c`. The `toArray()` method is used to convert the collection to an array so that we can access its elements by index.
