<code>assert !c.isEmpty() => \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < this.size(); this.get(i).equals(c.get(i));</code>

This assert statement checks that for every valid index `i` in the constructed list, the element at index `i` in the list is equal to the element at index `i` in the collection `c`, provided that `c` is not empty. Note that the condition `!c.isEmpty()` is used to ensure that `c.get(i)` is valid. However, since the constructor `addAll(c)` is called only if `c` is not null, we can assume that `c` is not null in this context.
